+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the inverse of the veterinarian directory: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. The clinic therefore publishes a specialty directory `[REQ-VET-003]` (stated 2026-08-11). It lists every specialty the clinic knows under the name that specialty is stored with, each with the veterinarians holding it. A veterinarian is shown by first name then last name. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on the page, which lists specialties rather than the whole roster. Every specialty appears on one page together, with no paging.
+
+The directory is read-only: NG-2 holds unchanged, and neither a specialty nor a veterinarian can be maintained here. The page is reachable by its address alone, and this requirement adds no navigation entry and no link from another page `[REQ-VET-003]`. Its wording follows the language requirement like every other page.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed under its stored name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each holder is shown by first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given every specialty the clinic knows, when the directory is opened, then all of them appear on one page, with no paging.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given any other page of the system, when it is rendered, then no navigation entry or link leads to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is listed with no veterinarian beside it, rather than left out.
+2. A clinic that knows no specialties yields an empty directory rather than a failure.
+3. The specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+4. The page carries the system's usual navigation, as `REQ-SYS-001` requires of every page. What this requirement omits is a link leading to the page, not the navigation on it.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
